### Real-World Test Cases

#### Test Case 1: The Base of the Sun’s Corona
* **Gas Pressure ($P_g$):** $\approx 0.1 \text{ Pa}$
* **Magnetic Field Strength ($B$):** $\approx 0.01 \text{ T}$ (100 Gauss)
* **Permeability of Free Space ($\mu_0$):** $4\pi \times 10^{-7} \text{ T}\cdot\text{m/A}$

$$P_m = \frac{(0.01)^2}{2 \times (4\pi \times 10^{-7})} \approx 39.8 \text{ Pa}$$

$$\beta = \frac{0.1 \text{ Pa}}{39.8 \text{ Pa}} \approx 0.0025$$

**Result:** $\beta \ll 1$ (Magnetism Rules). The plasma is forced to snap to magnetic field lines, launching as solar flares.

#### Test Case 2: Deep Inside Earth’s Liquid Outer Core
* **Confinement Pressure ($P_g$):** $\approx 1.35 \times 10^{11} \text{ Pa}$ (1.35 million atm)
* **Magnetic Field Strength ($B$):** $\approx 0.0025 \text{ T}$ (25 Gauss)

$$P_m = \frac{(0.0025)^2}{2 \times (4\pi \times 10^{-7})} \approx 2.49 \text{ Pa}$$

$$\beta = \frac{1.35 \times 10^{11} \text{ Pa}}{2.49 \text{ Pa}} \approx 5.42 \times 10^{10}$$

**Result:** $\beta \gg 1$ (Gravity Rules). Heavy iron flows purely based on gravity and rotation, dragging magnetic fields along with it.

| Environment | $\beta$ Value | Ultimate Commander | System Behavior |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Deep Planetary Core** | $\sim 10^{10}$ | Gravity / Mass | Pure fluid dynamics; mass dictates magnetic field shapes. |
| **The Surface Boundary** | $\sim 1.0$ | Dynamic Equilibrium | The crossroads; fields and mass actively fight for structural balance. |
| **Upper Atmosphere / Space** | $\sim 10^{-3}$ | Magnetism / Fields | Pure electromagnetics; mass is secondary. |

